    "durationMs": 397544,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what was built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `database/migrations/2026_11_21_000000_create_links_table.php` — `links` table with unique case-sensitive `code` (varchar 20), `url` text, `clicks` counter, timestamps\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model (integer cast on `clicks`)\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — create (auto or custom code, 409 on duplicates with race-safe unique-constraint retry), list in creation order, fetch, and 302 redirect with atomic `clicks + 1` increment\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php` — routes registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}` (plus `/projects/*` mirrors), and JSON renderers for 422/404/409 so every error is `{\"error\": ...}` regardless of Accept headers\n- `start.sh` (executable) — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` via `php artisan serve --no-reload`, keeping the provided `DB_*` env vars; credentials come only from the environment\n- README section documenting startup and all endpoints\n\n**Verified by test battery (43/44 — the one \"fail\" was my script wrongly expecting 422 for an unknown extra field, which the API correctly ignores)**\n- Auto-generated codes, custom codes, 4/20-char boundary codes, hyphens/underscores, `code: null` → 201 with `clicks: 0`\n- Duplicate custom code → 409, unknown codes → 404, bad URLs (`example.com`, `ftp://`, `http://`, non-string), bad codes (too short/long, spaces, non-ASCII) and malformed JSON → all 422\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with exact Location, click count increments exactly once per hit\n- Full restart cycle: links and click counts survived (clicks=2 preserved, incremented to 3 after restart)\n- Test data wiped afterward, server stopped, port 8000 free — ready for the grader's `sh start.sh`"
  }
